[TITLE]
AquaOptima dPHM-PINN Sprint 16 — small reference EPANET .inp fixture
in US-customary units. Five-node looped distribution sample:
one reservoir + four junctions, five pipes. GPM flow units,
Hazen-Williams head loss. Mirrors the structure of
epanet_reference_loop.inp but with feet/inches/GPM dimensions so the
Sprint 16 US-unit conversion path in the fallback parser is
exercised end-to-end.

US-customary EPANET convention (per the EPANET 2.2 user manual):
  - length in feet
  - diameter in inches
  - head/elevation in feet
  - demand/flow in the [OPTIONS] Units value (here GPM)

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID   Elev   Demand   Pattern
 J1   0.0    100.0    ;     ; 100 GPM consumer
 J2   0.0    150.0    ;     ; 150 GPM consumer
 J3   0.0    120.0    ;     ; 120 GPM consumer
 J4   0.0     80.0    ;     ;  80 GPM consumer

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID   Head   Pattern
 R1   300.0  ;          ; 300 ft fixed-head reservoir

[PIPES]
;ID   Node1   Node2   Length   Diameter   Roughness   MinorLoss   Status
 P1   R1      J1      1000.0   10.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN
 P2   J1      J2       800.0    8.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN
 P3   J2      J3       700.0    6.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN
 P4   J3      J4       650.0    6.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN
 P5   J1      J4       900.0    6.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN

[OPTIONS]
 Units                GPM
 Headloss             H-W

[END]
